  "details": "Version:968\nDescription of the bug:\nAfter the most recent update (968) when using full body tracking hands feel 'floaty' and they desync from the actual position of the controller. \nSteps to reproduce:\nOpen a menu that shows your controllers overlayed (settings, or pick up an object), you can see the position between the two shift as the hands move. This happens to some extent on all avatars, but is much more noticeable on some. The effect is also more noticeable when sitting down. \nAll of my testing was done with the arms far from full extension, on an Index HMD and controllers. I tried with both the new calibration and --legacy-fbt-calibrate flag and after a fresh reinstall.\nPreviously I had never noticed his behavior and hands not being where they should be, is something that is super noticeable.\nVideo: https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/384108535887298582/741203110592249906/2020-08-07_00-48-00_1_1.mp4",
